  "question": {
    "text": "The values of a for which the two points $(1, a, 1)$ and $(-3,0, a)$ lie on the opposite sides of the plane $3 x+4 y-12 z+13=0$, satisfy",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "4rvCW",
      "text": "\n$0 < a < \\frac{1}{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HG0eS",
      "text": "\n$-1 < a < 0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Ps4JM",
      "text": "\n$a < -1$ or $a < \\frac{1}{3}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "E911H",
      "text": "\n$a=0$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given equation of plane is\n$$\n3 x+4 y-12 z+13=0\n$$\n$(1, a, 1)$ and $(-3,0, a)$ satisfy the equation of plane.\n$\\therefore$ We have\n$3+4(a)-12+13=0$ and\n$3(-3)-12(a)+13=0$\n$\\Rightarrow 4+4 a=0$ and $4-12 a=0$\n$\\Rightarrow a=-1$ and $a=\\frac{1}{3}$\nSince, $(1, a, 1)$ and $(-3,0, a)$ lie on the opposite sides of the plane $\\therefore a=0$",
    "image": null
  },
